Short:        MUI-compatible GUI for Amigas (alpha)
Author:       David Le Corfec, AROS Development Team, Mushin contributors
Uploader:     stepan@coreboot.org (Stefan Reinauer)
Type:         util/libs
Version:      [VERSION]
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.1 or newer, 68000 or better
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

This alpha release is intended for testing and feedback.
Compatibility with MUI applications remains incomplete.

Mushin is a free, open source user interface library based on AROS Zune.
It aims to support classic MUI applications while staying responsive and
economical on ordinary m68k Amigas. Compatibility work is ongoing; the
version number does not imply complete MUI compatibility.

The full distribution includes:

- zunemaster.library and the alternative muimaster.library name
- Zune preferences editor and classic Workbench icons
- 13 native MCC/MCP plugins from BetterString, NList and TextEditor
- Preferences and plugin translations
- Example programs, SDK headers, documentation and corresponding source
- A version-aware Amiga Installer script with backups

No FPU is required. The system IEEE double math libraries are required.
Installation requires Amiga Installer 43 or newer, which is not bundled.

Extract the complete archive and double-click Install. The installer lets
you choose components and shows existing and bundled library versions.
Replacing muimaster.library affects applications using the standard MUI
library name. Back up your installation and reboot after replacing loaded
libraries. See the included ReadMe for installation and usage details.

The libraries use the same source under both names. Bundled third-party
classes open muimaster.library; using them alongside a different MUI
implementation has not been established as compatible.

Source builds support m68k-amigaos-gcc and retain the SAS/C build path.
The GCC build targets 68000 and software floating point. Diagnostic
tracing is disabled in normal builds. Physical-hardware performance and
application compatibility still need broader testing.

Mushin and its bundled components retain their original licenses and
copyright notices. See LICENSE and Docs in the archive.

Project: https://github.com/amigazen/mushin
Report issues: https://github.com/amigazen/mushin/issues
